Method add(String word) returns boolean: true if inserted new word, false if already present. It throws NullPointerException if word null. So the spec: after calling add(word), if word != null, then the trie contains(word) is true. Also if word null, exception thrown, but we can express as: \old(word != null) => this.contains(word). Actually we can't refer to word after exception; but we can express: word != null => this.contains(word). That's sufficient.

We may also need to consider that add returns boolean; but spec doesn't require about result. So assert: word != null => this.contains(word);

Make sure using \old? Not needed because contains after addition; we don't need old value. So final assert statement:

<code>assert word != null => this.contains(word);</code>

